<title>UK: Thames Water H1 pre-excep profits up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Thames Water H1 pre-excep profits up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>6 months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		37.9		   vs 39.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 11.2		   vs 9.2</p>
<p> Pretax		     176.0		  vs 165.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   621.5		  vs 599.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Results for water utility Thames Water Plc are on a pretax basis after exceptional items. The group said its pretax profit rose 15 percent to 188 million before exceptionals, which include a 12.2 million stg premium on the repurchase of convertible bonds.  </p>
<p>Thames bought back 10 percent of its shares on 31 July and it has also bought and cancelled 44 percent of its convertible bonds. It said earnings per share, adjusted for exceptional items were 41 pence versus 38.9p a year ago.</p>
<p> Operating result	 209.2		  vs 186.7</p>
<p> Interest payable	 13		     vs 26</p>
<p> Tax			  25.6		   vs 8.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 4</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 12</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
